---
import SectionHead from './SectionHead.astro';
---

<section id="about" class="scroll-mt-20 border-t border-ink-600/70 py-16 sm:py-24 lg:py-28">
  <div class="container-page">
    <SectionHead index="07" label="About" title="Builder first. The title came after." />

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-10 sm:mt-14 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-14">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-6 text-lead text-paper-dim lg:col-span-7" data-reveal>
        <p>
          I spent ten years writing Python and Django backends — the unglamorous middle of other people’s
          products. Somewhere in there the interesting problem stopped being the API and started being the
          whole thing: what the screen should say, what the business actually does at 8 pm on a Tuesday, and
          who has to be trusted with the data.
        </p>
        <p>
          The career ran through embedded electronics and sensors, fintech and banking, medical systems,
          casino gaming platforms, and AI / data / image pipelines — long before I owned the whole stack.
          Right now I am shipping <span class="text-paper">OrderEasy</span> (retailer and customer shop SaaS),
          <span class="text-paper">CiteBench</span> (case-law research desk), and
          <span class="text-paper">GSTSlip</span> (GST invoice capture). Backend, product surface, deploy, and
          the support reply when it breaks.
        </p>
        <p>
          I work from <span class="text-paper">Delhi NCR, India</span>, and I am a dad of two — which is the
          real reason the tooling has to be fast and the scope has to be honest.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a
            href="https://x.com/vin8003"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-paper underline decoration-ember decoration-2 underline-offset-4 transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-ember"
            >@vin8003</a
          > is a public lab notebook, not a brand channel. Progress, dead ends, and the occasional rewrite go up
          as they happen.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="flex flex-col gap-3 lg:col-span-5" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay:120ms">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-ink-600/80 bg-ink-850/60 p-5 sm:p-6">
          <p class="label-mono">Currently shipping</p>
          <ul class="mt-4 flex flex-col gap-3">
            {
              [
                { name: 'OrderEasy', note: 'Retailer + customer shop SaaS', dot: 'bg-mint' },
                { name: 'CiteBench', note: 'Case-law research desk for Indian practice', dot: 'bg-violet' },
                { name: 'GSTSlip', note: 'India GST invoice capture', dot: 'bg-amber' },
              ].map((p) => (
                <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
                  <span class={`mt-[0.45rem] size-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full ${p.dot}`} />
                  <span class="min-w-0">
                    <span class="block text-body font-medium text-paper">{p.name}</span>
                    <span class="block text-fine text-paper-faint">{p.note}</span>
                  </span>
                </li>
              ))
            }
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-dashed border-ink-500/80 p-5 sm:p-6">
          <p class="label-mono">Parked</p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-fine leading-relaxed text-paper-dim">
            An AI secretary for business phone lines. Designed, then shelved until the three above are properly
            done. Not shipped, not sold, not being pitched.
          </p>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
